      "text": "Martian Surface Robotics: Perseverance (Mars)\n\nRocket Lab Robotics hardware is actively operating on Mars aboard NASA’s Perseverance rover.\n\nMotiv Space Systems, acquired by Rocket Lab this year, designed and built Perseverance’s primary 2-meter, 5-joint robotic arm that positions coring tools directly against Martian rock faces using a 6-DOF force-torque sensor for sampling, and delivered the opto-mechanical system inclusive of zoom, focus, and filter-wheel for the Mastcam-Z science cameras.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "RocketLab",
